   "field": "ill_posed",
   "verifier": "The competency ('attested exclusivity never applies in value readers') and case_type 'positive' presuppose an undisputed ASSERTED answer listing both holders, which \u00a70.12 explicitly forbids for an exclusive office whose holders conflict; under the binding \u00a70.12 rule the answer is not undisputed, so the case_type should be 'disputed' and the competency premise is contradicted."
  },
  {
   "id": "X-021",
   "field": "contract_ambiguity",
   "verifier": "value_at \u00a73 ('Only declared slots apply; attested constraints never do', DI19 \u00a71) and \u00a72 (constraint_support always empty) versus \u00a70.12 ('an exclusive office whose holders conflict is never reported as undisputed by a value reader'). Reading 1 (value_at \u00a73 alone): status ASSERTED, values [pers-ward, pers-yeo], support supporting. Reading 2 (\u00a70.12, which overrides): the answer may not be undisputed; DISPUTED with both values and both claims conflicting. \u00a70.12 does not say which status replaces the undisputed one (DISPUTED is the only status consistent with values being held), nor how the constraint is cited when constraint_support must stay empty."
  },
